<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mayamara Satra</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Moamaria satra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mayamara Satra, often called the Moamaria satra, is a Vaishnavite monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> founded by Aniruddhadeva in the early seventeenth century. Its followers, many of them Morans, Kacharis and lower-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> peasants, were persecuted by Ahom kings who favoured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaktism">Shaktism</a>, and their resentment fuelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moamoria-rebellion">Moamoria rebellion</a> that began in 1769 and gravely weakened the Ahom kingdom.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Royal patronage of Shaktism alienated many Vaishnavite satras, and the persecution of the <b>Moamaria</b> monastery and its largely lower-caste and tribal followers set off the Moamoria rebellion in 1769.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ahom-kingdom">Ahom kingdom · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
